# Registry commands with no kernel rig case (`cargo xtask kernel-cases --coverage`). Every other
# command of `solidcraft-cli commands` (planned ones aside) must be run by some recipe.json under
# tests/kernel-cases/. One line a command: `<id>  <why it has no case>`; `#` starts a comment.
# Each section is sorted, with no id twice.
#
# Commands with no geometry to grade: the view, rendering, appearance, materials, selection, the
# browser, files and saving, documents, diagnostics, and component, parameter and timeline
# bookkeeping. Each is covered by the engine's and the UI's own tests. A command added since this
# folder stopped taking cases (tests/kernel-cases/CASES) is listed here too, its reason naming
# where it is tested: its kernel case in solidcore's corpus, or its test in its area's test file.

